Subject: Invalidating the global-variable cells moves the prototype epoch

What this does
  - `js_gv_cell_invalidate`, which every change to the global object's property structure (an add, a
    delete, a flag change) runs, now also moves `aot_pic_epoch`.

Why we need it
  A compiled function that reads a global through a register-VM global site keeps the property slot
  that site's cell names, taken once at the epoch its other cache cells were validated at. The slot
  is valid only for the generation the cell was filled at; the generation moved without the epoch
  moving, so the function would have kept a slot that a structure change had left behind. With this
  bump the function's existing epoch check after every call, and at the next entry, covers it. The
  value is still read from the slot on each use, so a plain value store to a global needs no watch.

Functions touched
  `js_gv_cell_invalidate`.

No.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -9125,0 +9126,5 @@
+#if QJS_REGVM
+    /* A compiled function holds the property slots of the global sites it read at some epoch;
+       they are valid only for the generation they were read at. */
+    rt->aot_pic_epoch++;
+#endif
